  "evidence": [
    {
      "id": "spec001:FACT-endpoints",
      "roomId": "spec001:R02",
      "subjectIds": [
        "spec001:PR012"
      ],
      "kind": "context",
      "text": "Known-good endpoints: Lift Sender A — known good; Workshop Receiver B — known good. Each passed the supplied local bench check before this exercise. Their known-good status is a declared scenario premise, not proof that the connecting path or an end-to-end service works. Source: signed bench cards on the topology relief table in The Titan's Workshop; PHY02 / C-SCOPE.",
      "ruleIds": [
        "spec001:PHY02"
      ],
      "requiresFreshMeasurement": false
    },
    {
      "id": "spec001:FACT-endpoint-a",
      "roomId": "spec001:R02",
      "subjectIds": [
        "spec001:PR012"
      ],
      "kind": "context",
      "text": "Lift Sender A — known good. Near endpoint: the labeled sender behind the lift call panel. Bench card A declares the local sender functional for this fictional exercise.",
      "ruleIds": [
        "spec001:PHY02"
      ],
      "requiresFreshMeasurement": false
    },
    {
      "id": "spec001:FACT-endpoint-b",
      "roomId": "spec001:R02",
      "subjectIds": [
        "spec001:PR012"
      ],
      "kind": "context",
      "text": "Workshop Receiver B — known good. Far endpoint: the receiver in the workshop dispatch console. Bench card B declares the local receiver functional for this fictional exercise.",
      "ruleIds": [
        "spec001:PHY02"
      ],
      "requiresFreshMeasurement": false
    },
    {
      "id": "spec001:FACT-path",
      "roomId": "spec001:R02",
      "subjectIds": [
        "spec001:PR012",
        "spec001:PR003",
        "spec001:PR014"
      ],
      "kind": "context",
      "text": "Physical path under test, in order: Lift Sender A → selected training conduit → workshop patch lead → Workshop Receiver B. Initial conduit: service loop, 95 m; alternative direct conduit: 85 m. The patch lead is 10 m in either configuration. The fixture declares compatible endpoints, media and terminations; the inspection grades length only. This path is the declared-path role of C-SCOPE, not the whole Iron City network. Source: topology relief table and matching conduit labels, The Titan's Workshop.",
      "ruleIds": [
        "spec001:PHY02",
        "spec001:PHY04"
      ],
      "requiresFreshMeasurement": false
    },
    {
      "id": "spec001:FACT-titan-clue",
      "roomId": "spec001:R02",
      "subjectIds": [
        "spec001:CH02"
      ],
      "kind": "context",
      "text": "Investigation scope. Inspect the physical path between known-good endpoints. Pin a testable hypothesis, keep it separate from observed evidence, and decide what observation would support or challenge it. Physical transmission represents bits; it does not select an IP route or verify an application login. Source: the Titan in The Titan's Workshop; PHY02 / S01, S02, S04.",
      "ruleIds": [
        "spec001:PHY02"
      ],
      "requiresFreshMeasurement": false
    }
  ],
